    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "We can use Vieta's formulas to relate the coefficients of the polynomial to the sum of the roots.\nIn this case, Vieta's formulas relate the sum of the roots $a + b + c$ to the coefficient of the $x^2$ term, which is $-\\frac{b}{a} = -\\frac{-3}{3} = 1$.\nSimilarly, Vieta's formulas relate the sum of the products of the roots taken two at a time $ab + ac + bc$ to the coefficient of the $x$ term, which is $\\frac{c}{a} = \\frac{\\frac{11}{3}}{3} = \\frac{11}{9}$.\nTherefore, $ab + ac + bc = 1 \\cdot \\frac{11}{9} = \\boxed{\\frac{11}{9}}$.The answer is: \\frac{11}{9}",
